{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Restart THIS Newbound instance, however it was launched - /proc/self/cgroup dispatch: a system systemd unit gets systemctl --no-block restart (sudo -n when not root), a user unit gets systemctl --user --no-block restart, and a plain command-line/session process self-respawns (a detached watcher waits for this pid to exit, then execs the identical cmdline in the identical cwd; output to runtime/restart.log). Returns OK/ERROR from the exit status before the process dies. Linux-only. NOTE: the command restarts the PROCESS THAT EXECUTES IT - called over the MCP bridge it restarts the MCP child, not the HTTP instance; call it through the HTTP instance (UI, /dev/restart_instance, or a peer's /peer/remote/uuid/dev/restart_instance).","groups":"admin","import":"use std::fs;\nuse std::process::Command;\nuse std::process::Stdio;\nuse std::os::unix::fs::MetadataExt;\n","params":[],"returntype":"String","type":"rust"},"id":"zosxwm1a052c55690j10","readers":["admin"],"time":1788095091574,"username":"system","writers":[]}